  "body_html": "<p>By <a href=\"https://plus.google.com/+MadsStoumannDK?rel=author\">Mads Stoumann</a></p>\n<p>I have a large collection of vinyl records, and music is an important part of my life. Hence my experiment today, which is to (re-) create a spinning vinyl record using only CSS.</p>\n<p>I&#8217;ve created various effects in the past, using Flash, canvas and SVG &mdash; but I wanted to see what could be accomplished with just CSS. And it looks pretty neat!</p>\n<p>I can&#8217;t really see a use-case for it, except a (very different!) icon for a music-player.</p>\n<p>Hope you like it.</p>\n<div class=\"embed-codepen\"><iframe title=\"Pure CSS Record (Vinyl)\" id=\"cp_embed_GqKyLK\" src=\"https://codepen.io/stoumann/embed/preview/GqKyLK?default-tabs=css%2Cresult&amp;height=300&amp;host=https%3A%2F%2Fcodepen.io&amp;slug-hash=GqKyLK\" scrolling=\"no\" frameborder=\"0\" height=\"300\" allowtransparency=\"true\" allowfullscreen=\"true\" allowpaymentrequest=\"true\" class=\"cp_embed_iframe\" style=\"width: 100%; overflow: hidden;\"></iframe></div>\n<p>Happy coding!</p>",
